          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+6y+z &=18 \\\\ 6x-36y-6z &=-108 \\\\ -4x+24y+4z &=72\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 1 & 18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6 & 1 & 18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 6 & -36 & -6 & -108 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 24 & 4 & 72\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 & -1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
