          ":question/id": "0357dea2-ef92-567a-97bc-c0ef4a81db45",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-131638",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z &=1 \\\\ -4x-8y+12z &=-4 \\\\ 2x+4y-6z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -8 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -8 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
